{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1511970487,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzc4MDQxMjk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2006","origin":"github"},"title":"Implement `datalad serve -d \u003cpath\u003e`","message":"We are almost there.\n\nLargely string based arguments to all API functions. Return values are essentialy JSON (if requested).\n\nWe only need a few extra lines (with e.g. flask) to be able to make dataset query/manipulation accessible via a web-request API.\n\nOnce done, we can make sure that our coming extensions of web stuff still go through the same underlying API, and help further standardizing and homogenizing our structures.\n\nHaving another interface without an attached console should also help to bring more clarity to the handling of messaging and outputs.\n\nNB: flask can be nicely integrated with proper webservers via WSGI, while also coming with a simple built-in devserver.","files":null}]}